{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-ecc-11-1","title":"Ecclesiastes 11:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Directions for charity. 7 Death in life, 9 and the day ofjudgment in the days of youth, are to be thought on.</p>\n<p>Cast.That is, says Bp. Lowth, \"Sow thy seed or corn on the face of the waters;\" in plain terms, sow without any hope of a harvest: do good even to them on whom your benefactions seem thrown away. Dr. Jebb has well illustrated it by the following passages:</p>\n<p>\"Vain are the favours done to vicious men; Not vainer 'tis to sow the foaming deep. The deep no pleasant harvest shall afford, Nor will the wicked ever make return.\"</p>\n<p>\"To befriend the wicked is like sowing in the sea.\" These, indeed, invert this precept; nor is it extraordinary that they should;</p>\n<p>\"The one, frail human power alone produced, The other, God.\"</p>\n<p>thy bread. De 15:7-11; Pr 11:24,25; 22:9; Isa 32:8 waters. Heb. face of the waters. Isa 32:20 for. 6; De 15:10; Ps 41:1,2; 126:5,6; Pr 11:18; 19:17; Mt 10:13,42; 25:40 Lu 14:14; 2Co 9:6; Ga 6:8-10; Heb 6:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ecc-11-2","title":"Ecclesiastes 11:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>a portion. Ne 8:10; Es 9:19,22; Ps 112:9; Lu 6:30-35; 1Ti 6:18,19 seven. Job 5:19; Pr 6:16; Mic 5:5; Mt 18:22; Lu 17:4 for. Da 4:27; Ac 11:28-30; Ga 6:1; Eph 5:16; Heb 13:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ecc-11-3","title":"Ecclesiastes 11:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>the clouds. 1Ki 18:45; Ps 65:9-13; Isa 55:10,11; 1Jo 3:17 if the tree. Mt 3:10; Lu 13:7; 16:22-26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ecc-11-4","title":"Ecclesiastes 11:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>Pr 3:27; 20:4; 22:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ecc-11-5","title":"Ecclesiastes 11:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>thou knowest not what. Joh 3:8 nor. Ps 139:14,15 even. 7:24; 8:17; Job 5:9; 26:5-14; 36:24-33; 37:23; 38:4-41; 39:1-41:34 Ps 40:5; 92:5; 104:24; Isa 40:28; Ro 11:33</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ecc-11-6","title":"Ecclesiastes 11:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>sow. 9:10; Isa 55:10; Ho 10:12; Mr 4:26-29; Joh 4:36-38; 2Co 9:6 2Ti 4:2 thou knowest. 9:1; Hag 1:6-11; 2:17-19; Zec 8:11,12; Ac 11:20,21; 1Co 3:5-7 2Co 9:10,11 prosper. Heb. be right.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ecc-11-7","title":"Ecclesiastes 11:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>the light. Job 33:28,30; Ps 56:13; Pr 15:30; 29:13 a pleasant. 7:11; Ps 84:11; Mt 5:45</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ecc-11-8","title":"Ecclesiastes 11:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>if a man. 6:6; 8:12 rejoice. 3:12,13; 5:18-20; 8:15 yet. 7:14; 12:1-5; De 32:29; Job 10:22; 14:10; 15:23; 18:18; Jer 13:16 Joe 2:2; Mt 22:13; Joh 12:35; Jude 1:18 All that. 2:1-11,15,17,19,21-23,26; 4:8,16; 5:15,16; 6:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ecc-11-9","title":"Ecclesiastes 11:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>Rejoice. 1Ki 18:27; 22:15; Lu 15:12,13 in thy youth. 12:1; 1Ki 18:12; La 3:27 walk. Nu 15:30; 22:32; De 29:19; Job 31:7; Ps 81:12; Jer 7:24; 23:17 Jer 44:16,17; Ac 14:16; Eph 2:2,3; 1Pe 4:3,4 in the sight. 2:10; Ge 3:6; 6:2; Jos 7:21; 2Sa 11:2-4; Mt 5:28; 1Jo 2:15,16 know. 3:17; 12:14; Ps 50:4-6; Ac 17:30,31; 24:25; Ro 2:5-11; 14:10 1Co 4:5; 2Co 5:10; 2Pe 3:7; Heb 9:27; Re 20:12-15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ecc-11-10","title":"Ecclesiastes 11:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>remove. 12:1; Job 13:26; Ps 25:7; 2Pe 3:11-14 sorrow. or, anger. Ps 90:7-11 and put. Job 20:11; 2Co 7:1; 2Ti 2:22 for. 1:2,14; Ps 39:5; Pr 22:15</p>"}]}